              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IPLawyerMom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the recipe closely and it was pretty good! Modifications: browned the onion the skillet after I browned the turkey, and added a clove of minced garlic to the onions. Also, I let the mixture stay in the crockpot on high for longer (about 35 minutes) and put the cheese on top for about 20 minutes. I took a photo with the cheese only on 1/2 before it melted, so that you can see what it looks like without the cheese covering it. Big hit with the hubby and little ones. It is slightly sweet, but the family liked that. :)",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-14T20:31:00.690Z"
